justice shall fall upon the world men  the Army's right and shadow will collide  across the fields of eternity  [Music]  more than anything Diablo 3 eternal  collection proves just how well  blizzards action-rpg has aged six years  after its original release the dungeon  crawler remains as rewarding as ever and  despite a few technical concessions it  has found yet another welcoming home on  Nintendo's portable console for those  unfamiliar with blizzards 2012 loot fest  Diablo 3 places you in the shoes of a  super-powered demon slayer in a hellish  gothic world you explore five disparate  regions from a top-down view upgrading  your character and earning new loot as  you battle the lords of the underworld  and their monstrous swarms with the  eternal collection Diablo 3 includes  every expansion every character every  quality of life improvement the RPG has  ever implemented one of the more notable  options here is the ability to play  adventure mode right from the start  eliminating the need to slog through the  slower paced story out of necessity of  course incoming to Nintendo switch  Diablo 3 has also become a portable game  and it works it works incredibly well in  fact I can imagine few games better  suited for a handheld port so much of  Diablo 3 plays best in short bursts from  the 10-minute chase for that next  legendary item to the satisfying flow of  a challenge rift it's another testament  to the novelty of Nintendo's console yes  but also the elegance of Diablo 3's  design as was the case with Diablo  threes previous jump to ps4 and Xbox one  the mechanical leap to switch is  painless and fluid it's still just as  easy to rely on muscle memory while you  focused on the kaleidoscopic display of  magic and fire when it comes to visual  fidelity Blizzard ensured that Diablo 3  on switch runs at 60 frames across the  board  aside from rare occasions when elemental  effects didn't animate on screen the  eternal collection is remarkably clean  the frame rate is equally stable in  handheld mode and online and crunching  those mobs is just as satisfying as it's  ever been  the eternal collections resolution on  the other hand is a bit more muddled in  the switches dock mode Diablo 3 looks  aggressively fine or at least as good as  any other six year old isometric game in  handheld mode 720p resolution how  things get cloudier there's a slight  haze over everything making character  models look more like mirages than  actual figures handheld modes jagged  edges and foggy panoramas aren't massive  flaws by any means but after playing for  long periods in docked mode they tend to  stand out what they don't do however is  detract from Diablos  thrilling combat and of course in true  series tradition that combat is often  more thrilling with a friend or too few  cooperative experiences compared to a  monk demon hunter barbarian and wizard  working in concert to whittle down mobs  one demon at a time it's a special  thrill to see my character build factor  into a larger group and an even better  one to see how that group dynamics  subtly changes how I play as with  previous console iterations of Diablo 3  the eternal collection allows up to 4  players on one console at a time item  management is less satisfying in this  scenario as you're either a quick  equipping new loot without appreciating  its subtleties or pausing the game for  the entire party just so you can boost  your damage by 100 points the radial  menus are also still as imprecise as  ever but I'm hard-pressed to think of a  better solution without a mouse and  keyboard the eternal collection brings  the additional ease of playing via land  connection on each player's respective  switch it's helpful to have the camera  focused solely on your character  especially in Diablo 3's more hectic  moments but I still couldn't help  preferring local co-op there's something  novel even nostalgic about playing on  the same screen watching the same chaos  unfold as the person next to you  regardless Diablo 3 on switch allows for  several methods of playing with friends  and whatever your preference might be  the experience still holds up like the  best games Diablo 3 has gotten better  with time and despite a few setbacks the  switch is now my preferred home for the  extraordinary RPG it includes every  major improvement Blizzard has made to  the formula with the added handheld  versatility every switch port offers  Diablo 3 is a game about long-term goals  accomplished in short thrilling bursts  I have spent six years enjoying it and  will likely spend 6 years more I came  into the eternal collection expecting a  eulogy for one of my favorite games but  instead I stumbled upon a celebration  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

